# <type>(<scope>)!: <subject>
#
# type:    feat, fix, docs, test, refactor, style, build, ci, chore
# scope:   optional, and then one of these:
#            Library     auth, client, diagnostics, errors, files,
#                        options, pages, revisions
#            Tests       smoke, tests
#            Build       deps, package, release, sln
#            Repository  commit-check, dependabot, github, scripts
#            Docs        contributing, docs, readme, site
#            Editor      editorconfig, rider
# !:       only for a breaking change, and then always, with a
#          BREAKING CHANGE: footer below
# subject: imperative (add, not Added or Adds), starting with a
#          lowercase letter, no trailing period; the whole header is at
#          most 72 characters
#
# Body (optional), after a blank line: what changed and why, not how.
# Wrap it at 72 characters; only a line holding a URL or a trailer such
# as Co-authored-by: may run longer.
#
# Footers (optional):
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <what breaks and how to migrate>
#       spelled with a space, not a hyphen, and only with the ! above
#   Fixes #<issue>
#       one per issue, each on a line of its own after a blank line or
#       another Fixes line; no other wording may close an issue, such as
#       Closes #N, Fixes: #N or a fixes #N inside a sentence
#
# The full convention is in CONTRIBUTING.md.
